  "prefLabel": "Pes 505.03 Woodland Areas Greater than 50 Acres",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pes 505.03 Woodland Areas Greater than 50 Acres. No pesticide shall be applied by any person to woodland areas exceeding 50 acres without being in possession of a special permit issued by the division according to procedures set forth in Pes 505.05 (a) through (d) and upon consultation with the state forester and the director of the fish and game department. Application for approval shall be made on “Form ROW/WL Special Permit Application-Right-of-Way/Woodland” and shall include the information in Pes 505.05(d).\n\nSource. #150, eff 1-9-74; ss by #2209, eff 12-13-82; ss by #2781, eff 7-26-84; ss by #4867, eff 7-19-90; ss by #6258, eff 5-30-96; ss by #6944, eff 2-24-99; ss by #7890, eff 5-19-03; ss by #8131, eff 8-13-04; ss by #10333, eff 5-10-13; ss by #14064, eff 8-22-24",
